//! Zap structured adapter: subscribes to harness IPC and renders Blocks.
//!
//! This binary connects to the harness Unix socket, streams events, and renders
//! structured Blocks to stdout. It translates typed events (Intent, Plan, Tool,
//! Approval, Agent) into visual Blocks with OSC sequences for Zap terminal.
//!
//! ## Current implementation (v0.3 step 2/4)
//!
//! - Basic block rendering with visual separators
//! - OSC escape sequences for terminal notifications:
//!   - OSC 777 for generic notifications (widely supported)
//!   - OSC 9 for iTerm2/Windows Terminal compatibility
//!   - OSC 0 for window title updates
//! - State transition notifications: Idle → Running → NeedsApproval → Completed
//! - Event notifications: approvals, errors, backend status
//!
//! ## TODO: Structured blocks protocol (next step)
//!
//! The next iteration will implement a richer structured blocks protocol:
//! - Diff rendering with syntax highlighting
//! - Interactive approval buttons (click to approve/reject)
//! - Live streaming agent chunks (without block borders)
//! - Attachment preview links
//! - Status bar integration
//!
//! This will likely require:
//! - Custom escape sequences or terminal-specific protocols
//! - Zap-specific extensions if standard protocols are insufficient
//! - Bidirectional IPC for button clicks → harness approval resolution

